A job's standard input from make text: $(amk.stdin text), expanded in a recipe line,
feeds the text to the command on that line through a pipe, written by a detached helper
so the text may be any size. The pipe is bound to the recipe line it was expanded in,
by the target's variable set and the line's index, so lines and targets that interleave
under -j each get their own. With it, an engine's flag form reads its program from
standard input when the argument is a lone dash, so an imported target's program reaches
its engine with no file and no argument limit.

